            <ArticleTitle>Complete Genome Sequence of Lactobacillus plantarum 10CH, a Potential Probiotic Lactic Acid Bacterium with Potent Antimicrobial Activity.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01398-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01398-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lactobacillus plantarum 10CH is a bacteriocin-producing potential probiotic lactic acid bacterium (LAB) strain isolated from cheese. Its complete nucleotide sequence shows a single circular chromosome of 3.3 Mb, with a G+C content of 44.51%, a 25-gene plantaricin bacteriocin gene cluster, and the absence of recognized virulence factors.</AbstractText>
